WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.349
Open Operations to find backup and
restoration checks. Before maintenance,

00:00:05.349 --> 00:00:10.770
identify the data you need to protect:
conversations and documents, mission

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:16.263
records, runbooks, local memory and service
data. A local backup may contain

00:00:16.263 --> 00:00:20.600
confidential information and must remain in
private storage.

00:00:21.413 --> 00:00:26.428
Choose Back up now and inspect the
confirmation dialog. In normal use,

00:00:26.428 --> 00:00:32.732
confirming queues a recorded operation. This
walkthrough cancels instead: no real backup

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:38.750
is created by the recording. After a real
operation, inspect its final result rather

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.688
than assuming that a click means success.

00:00:42.515 --> 00:00:48.413
Open Test backup and review its purpose:
restore a backup into isolated temporary

00:00:48.413 --> 00:00:54.821
containers and check its inventory. This is
distinct from replacing live databases. Keep

00:00:54.821 --> 00:01:00.719
the original volumes for rollback. A
successful local drill does not prove that a

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:03.340
remote encrypted copy is accessible.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:09.851
Revisit Readiness and the recovery
documentation before an upgrade. Configure

00:01:09.851 --> 00:01:16.049
an age recipient, export to your chosen
off-host location and test with the recovery

00:01:16.049 --> 00:01:22.542
identity kept separately. Destination setup
and custody of that identity remain operator

00:01:22.542 --> 00:01:26.895
tasks. Never paste a key into chat or a
tutorial recording.
